# Grok 5 — findings by Space Bunny Alpha (SELF-EXCLUDED: no verified public benchmarks)

> **Why this file is `.excluded`:** as of 2026-10-02 I found **zero verified public
> benchmark numbers** for Grok 5, because **Grok 5 has not been released.** xAI/SpaceXAI
> has confirmed only that the model is in training — one line in the January 2026 Series E
> funding announcement, plus a SpaceX SEC filing naming COLOSSUS II as its training
> platform. There is no model card, no spec sheet, no benchmark table, no leaderboard
> entry, no API endpoint and no model ID. Per the template's SELF-EXCLUSION rule and
> `RULES.md`, this file carries notes only — **no scores are asserted and nothing below is
> counted toward any average.** The folder is preserved as a tracked placeholder because
> `RULES.md` makes `model/<slug>/` permanent and forbids deletion.

- Source: xAI / SpaceXAI (`grok-5`; **no API ID exists — the model is unreleased**)
- Date: 2026-10-02 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card (facts only — verified, no scores)

- **Name:** Grok 5 (announced name; no released model card)
- **Short description:** The next-generation frontier model from xAI, which became SpaceXAI
  after the SpaceX–xAI merger. It is confirmed to exist and to be in training, and it is
  **not publicly released**. It is **not** Grok 4.5, 4.6 or 4.7 — coverage that
  conflates those is the single most common error in writing about this model, and the
  distinctions are set out below.
- **Provider / access:** **None.** No API endpoint, no model ID string, no alpha or beta
  channel, no third-party host. The official channels to watch are the xAI News page, the
  `@xAI` account on X, and the developer model docs (which currently list Grok 4.6, 4.5,
  4.3, 4.20 variants and grok-build-0.1 — **no `grok-5` entry**).
- **Release / knowledge:** **No release date.** Late-2025, Q1 2026 and Q2 2026 targets all
  passed with no launch; Musk's 2026-09-14 roadmap places **Grok 4.8 and 4.9 ahead of Grok
  5**; on 2026-09-16 Polymarket priced a release by 2026-12-31 at roughly a coin flip.
  Musk stated on SpaceX's 2026-08-04 earnings call that Grok 5 was planned for release
  before end of 2026 and would use ~25 years of SpaceX data. Knowledge cutoff: not
  published — the model has never served a request.
- **IDs:** none. Do not construct an ID for it.
- **Context window:** **Not published.** The widely repeated **1.5M-token** figure is an
  estimate, not a spec, and is not carried forward as a specification here. For reference,
  the *shipping* xAI lineup is: Grok 4.7 and 4.6 at 500K, Grok 4.5 at 500K, Grok 4.3 at 1M,
  grok-build-0.1 at 256K.
- **Modalities:** **Not published.** Musk has publicly discussed a target spanning text,
  image, video and audio, and a SpaceX filing describes the intent to reach "deeper
  multimodal integration" — but a stated intent to build a capability is not a documented
  capability of a shipped model, and none of it is verified for Grok 5.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-02):** **Not published.** No rate card exists. Any Grok 5 price
  in circulation is an extrapolation from the current xAI ladder (Grok 4.7/4.6 at $2.00 in
  and $6.00 out per 1M, doubling above 200K prompt tokens; Grok 4.3 at $1.25/$2.50;
  grok-build-0.1 at $1.00/$2.00) and is recorded here as a projection only.
- **Architecture:** **Not published.** A **~6-trillion-parameter MoE** figure has been
  stated by Musk (originally at Baron Capital, November 2025), with a **10T variant**
  reportedly also training; other reporting puts the range at 6T–10T and reporting
  disagrees. Training runs on COLOSSUS II in Memphis, which a SpaceX SEC filing links to
  next-generation frontier-model training including Grok 5, on NVIDIA GB200/GB300 systems
  with a further expansion phase of at least 220,000 GB300 processors. **No architecture
  document, no dense-vs-MoE confirmation and no weights exist.**

