### Negative-findings notes (what I checked, and what each source actually says)

- **xAI developer model docs** (docs.x.ai/developers/models) — the authoritative
  availability-and-pricing reference. Lists grok-4.6, grok-4.5, grok-4.3,
  grok-4.20-0309-reasoning / -non-reasoning, grok-4.20-multi-agent-0309 and
  grok-build-0.1, with context windows and per-1M rates. **There is no `grok-5` row.**
  This is the single most load-bearing negative finding in this file.
- **xAI January 2026 Series E funding announcement** — the only official statement that
  Grok 5 exists: it was in training. One sentence, no specifications.
- **SpaceX SEC filing** — links COLOSSUS II to next-generation frontier-model training
  including Grok 5, and describes deeper multimodal integration and better specialised-domain
  performance as *goals*, plus a next expansion phase of at least 220,000 GB300 processors
  and over 400 MW.
- **SpaceX 2026-08-04 earnings call** — Musk: release intended before end of 2026, trained
  on ~25 years of SpaceX data. A target, not a date, and not a benchmark.
- **Musk on X, 2026-09-14** — "Grok 4.8, which is a 2.5T model trained with our new C++
  software stack, will finish training this week and start RL"; asked how close 4.8 would
  get to AGI: "That will be Grok 5." A roadmap position with no benchmark, no definition
  of AGI and no date attached.
- **geotoolbox.ai Grok 5 tracker (September 2026)** — the most disciplined secondary source
  found. Separates confirmed from estimated, and lists five signals that would constitute a
  real launch: a `grok-5` entry in the xAI model docs; an official model or system card; a
  benchmark or leaderboard entry (LMArena, SWE-bench); a launch post from `@xAI` rather than
  a one-line Musk reply; and a published price. **None of the five is present.**
- **felloai.com (updated 2026-09-23)** and **kie.ai** — both confirm the slippage pattern
  (late-2025, Q1 2026 and Q2 2026 windows all closed empty) and both state the Q1/Q2/Q3
  targeting has no confirmed successor date. kie.ai is explicit that there is no confirmed
  alpha, beta, API endpoint or model ID string, and that no third-party platform hosts the
  model.
- **buildbevy.com (2026-08-21)** — itemises what xAI has *not* confirmed: exact parameter
  count, architecture, training dataset, benchmark scores, context window, pricing, release
  date.
- **Polymarket, 2026-09-16** — priced a Grok 5 release by 2026-12-31 at roughly a coin
  flip. Useful only as a statement about the absence of confidence.
- **tesorb.com (2026-07-08)** — reports two MoE variants training (6T and 10T) on roughly
  520,000 GB200s and 30,000 GB300s, and notes a "Project Valis" leak circulating that AI
  trackers flag as unreliable. The leak is **not** used.
- **Adjacent shipped models must not be substituted.** Grok 4.5 (2026-07-08), Grok 4.6
  (2026-08-12) and Grok 4.7 (2026-09-21) are real, benchmarked models with published rows
  — and Grok 4.7 is the current flagship, at AA Intelligence Index 46.3 (v4.3.2) vs Grok
  4.6's 44.3. **None of their numbers, context windows or prices are Grok 5's.** The
  recurring pattern in secondary coverage is to present 4.7's results under a Grok 5
  heading; that substitution is refused here.
- **Naming trap, recorded because it recurs in sources:** "Grok V9" / "V9-Medium" is the
  ~1.5T Cursor-trained model that shipped **as Grok 4.5**, not as Grok 5. Grok 5 is the
  separate, much larger model still in training.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

- **Not scored.** No verified public benchmark exists for Grok 5 as of 2026-10-02 — the
  model has not been released, so per the template's SELF-EXCLUSION rule no Tool use /
  Reasoning / Context window / Multimodal / Coding / Cost efficiency / Overall numbers are
  asserted here. Writing placeholder scores would turn a training run into invented quality
  evidence and drag the mean for every reader.
- The four things that *are* verified and worth carrying forward: **the model exists and is
  in training**; **COLOSSUS II in Memphis is its training platform** (SpaceX SEC filing);
  **Musk has publicly discussed ~6T parameters and a before-end-of-2026 release target**;
  and **no official date, spec, card, price or benchmark has been published.** None of these
  is a capability measurement.
- What a future report should pick up, in priority order: (1) a `grok-5` row in the xAI
  model docs, which is the availability precondition for everything else; (2) an official
  model or system card with an architecture and context window; (3) any benchmark or
  leaderboard row (Artificial Analysis, LMArena, SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench); (4) a
  published rate card; (5) a reproducible third-party run. When (1) and (3) land, a scored
  `.md` should be written and this file retired.

